BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Montclair State University
CATEGORIES:ThoughtfulLearning
CATEGORIES:Academic/Educational/Intellectual
DESCRIPTION:A DOCUMENTARY DIRECTED BY VALERIO CIRIACI (2025\, Awen Films\,
  90mins)\nNov. 10 / 6:00 PM University Hall Conference Center\, 7th Floor
 \nScreening followed by an in-person conversation with the director \nMod
 erated by Teresa Fiore (Inserra Chair\, Italian\, CHSS) and Anthony Pembe
 rton (Film\, CCOM) with opening remarks by Mila Tenaglia (N.I.C.E.)\n \nE
 LVIRA NOTARI: BEYOND SILENCE is a feature documentary chronicling the lif
 e and work of Elvira Notari (1875-1946)\, Italy's first woman film direct
 or. Despite directing hundreds of silent films that captivated audiences 
 from Naples to New York\, Elvira was relegated to the margins of film his
 tory for half a century. Her films\, poised between realism and staged dr
 ama\, were deeply rooted in Neapolitan folklore. A woman in a man’s world
 \, her works were targeted by Fascist censorship yet found the embrace of
  audiences on both sides of the Atlantic. The documentary interweaves voi
 ces of those who celebrate her legacy today – from the experts who redisc
 overed her films to contemporary artists reimagining her vision through n
 ew works – to resurrect Elvira’s singular vision. More than a biography\,
  Elvira Notari: Beyond Silence is a prismatic portrait of an artist who c
 ontinues to inspire new creative pathways.\n \nSelect recognitions: Offic
 ial Selection - Venice Classics at the 82nd Venice International Film Fes
 tival (World Premiere)\; Best Documentary\, Globo d’Oro 2026\; Shortliste
 d Best Documentary\, David di Donatello 2026\; Finalist – Documentary on 
 Cinema\, Performing Arts & Culture\, Nastri d’Argento 2026.\nA Parallelo 
 41 Produzioni and Awen Films co-production with Cinecittà. With support f
 rom the Italian Ministry of Culture\, Film Commission Regione Campania\, 
 City of Naples\, in collaboration with Casa Italiana Zerilli-Marimò at NY
 U and Archivio Audiovisivo del movimento operaio e democratico.\n \nValer
 io Ciriaci - director\nOriginally from Rome\, Valerio moved to New York i
 n 2011 to attend courses at New York Film Academy. In 2013 he co-founded 
 Awen Films\, a production company specializing in  independent documentar
 ies with a focus on transnational and historical topics. As director\, hi
 s filmography highlights include If Only I Were That Warrior (Globo d’Oro
  2016\, aired on Rai Storia)\; Mister Wonderland (‘Il Cinemino’ prize at 
 Festival dei Popoli\, aired on Rai\, and PBS)\; and Stonebreakers (Honora
 ble Mention\, Audience Award\, and the ‘Imperdibili’ prize at Festival de
 i Popoli)\, which has been screened over 100 times at leading cinemas and
  international cultural institutions. His latest feature\, Elvira Notari:
  Beyond Silence\, premiered at the 82nd Venice International Film Festiva
 l in the Classics section.\n \nThe event is co-organized and co-sponsored
  by NICE. (New Italian Cinema Events) and the Inserra Chair in Italian an
 d Italian American Studies (Italian Program\, Global Cultural Studies Dep
 artment\, College of the Humanities and Social Sciences)\, and the Animat
 ion\, Film and Television program\, College of Communication and Media).\
 n \nThe event is moderated by Prof. Teresa Fiore (Inserra Chair in Italia
 n and Italian American Studies\, Global Cultural Studies Dept.\, College 
 of the Humanities and Social Sciences) and Prof. Anthony Pemberton (Anima
 tion\, Film and Television Dept.\, College of Communication and Media) wi
 th opening remarks by Mila Tenaglia (Executive Director\, N.I.C.E.\, an o
 rganization celebrating its 36th edition in the United States under the d
 irection of its founder\, Viviana del Bianco).\n\nHosted by: College of H
 umanities and Social Sciences (CHSS)\n\nAdditional Information can be fou
 nd at: https://montclair.campuslabs.com/engage/event/12942311
DTEND:20261111T013000Z
DTSTAMP:20261107T055208Z
DTSTART:20261110T230000Z
GEO:40.859760;-74.199750
LOCATION:University Hall Conference Center\, 7th Floor
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Elvira Notari: Beyond Silence - Documentary Screening and Q&A with
  Director Valerio Ciriaci
