DESCRIPTION:Join us for a panel discussion and Q&A featuring experts in Po
 litical Science and Communication as they discuss the 2026 midterm electi
 ons. Attendees will have the opportunity to ask questions about the role 
 of Latino voters\, gender dynamics\, the media\, artificial intelligence 
 (AI)\, and presidential politics.  \nDate: November 11\, 2026 Time: 2:30–
 3:30 p.m. Location: Presentation Hall\, College of Communication and Medi
 a Panelists: Dr. Yoshira Macias Mejía\, Political Science Dr. Joel Penney
 \, Communication Dr. Jackie Vimo\, Political Science Moderator: Dr. Fanny
  Lauby\, Political Science \nContact Information: Dr. Fanny Lauby laubyf@
 montclair.edu \nCo-Sponsors: The Department of Political Science\, Law\, 
 History\, and Anthropology\; the Department of Communication and Media St
 udies\; and the Political Science Club.\n\nHosted by: College of Humaniti
 es and Social Sciences (CHSS)\n\nAdditional Information can be found at: 
 https://montclair.campuslabs.com/engage/event/12920544
