DESCRIPTION:CLaSE invites members of the Montclair State University commun
 ity and the broader public to participate in Learning in Circle: English 
 for the Community\, beginning Thursday\, September 17.\nThis 10-week work
 shop series provides a welcoming and supportive environment for adult lea
 rners who want to strengthen their English conversation and comprehension
  skills through practical\, interactive activities. Workshops are open to
  students\, families\, and community members from outside the University.
 \nThursdays\, beginning September 176–7:30 p.m.Schmitt Hall\, Room 10410-
 week series\nThe workshops are free and open to the community\, but regis
 tration is required by contacting calarotaa@montclair.edu. We invite anyo
 ne interested in improving their English skills to join us and learn in c
 ommunity! \n\nHosted by: Center for Latino Heritage & Spanish Language Ex
 cellence\n\nAdditional Information can be found at: https://montclair.cam
 puslabs.com/engage/event/12663657
