BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Montclair State University
CATEGORIES:ThoughtfulLearning
CATEGORIES:Workshop
DESCRIPTION:\nHow can we help students become more discerning\, critical\,
  and responsible users of information in the age of AI? Join Bonnie Fong 
 (Director\, Bloomfield College Library) for an interactive professional d
 evelopment opportunity focused on Critical Information Literacy and AI Li
 teracy. We will discuss effective ways we can teach students how to:\n\nn
 avigate and use information in an increasingly AI-driven information land
 scape\, recognizing the limitations of AI tools and AI-generated content\
 ; \ncritically evaluate information\, identifying possible bias and refle
 cting on the existing economic\, political\, social\, and cultural struct
 ures that impact information creation\, dissemination\, and access\; and\
 nincorporate responsible and thoughtful AI practices into their academic 
 work and possibly their life.\n\nParticipants will be introduced to the t
 eaching resources that Bonnie and Melissa John (Research & Instruction Li
 brarian) developed - a rubric with accompanying instructional activities 
 with possible assessments - and will be invited to share their own approa
 ches to teaching critical information literacy skills and AI literacy.  T
 hey will be provided with the opportunity to consider how they might adap
 t these for use in their own courses\, with the goal of leaving the sessi
 on with fresh ideas and perhaps an updated assignment ready to bring back
  to their classroom.\nThis workshop is sponsored by the Bloomfield Colleg
 e Faculty Professional Development Committee\, Office of Faculty Excellen
 ce\, and University Libraries.\nFaculty and instructors: Be sure to regis
 ter below and bring an existing assignment (or two) to the Zoom session!\
 n\nRelated LibGuide: Educated Citizenry (Critical Information Literacy) b
 y Bonnie Fong\nRegister Here: https://montclair.libcal.com/event/17939816
 \n\nHosted by: Sprague Library\n\nOnline Location: https://montclair.libc
 al.com/event/17939816\n\nAdditional Information can be found at: https://
 montclair.campuslabs.com/engage/event/12943178
DTEND:20261113T170000Z
DTSTAMP:20261107T055208Z
DTSTART:20261113T160000Z
LOCATION:Online
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Critical Information Literacy and AI Literacy
UID:https://montclair.campuslabs.com/engage/event/12943178
URL:https://montclair.campuslabs.com/engage/event/12943178
X-HOSTS:Sprague Library
END:VEVENT
