 hern Territory in 1929\, the film explores the experiences of Aboriginal 
 Australians under colonial rule and raises important questions about just
 ice\, racism\, cultural identity\, and belonging.This screening invites s
 tudents to broaden their global perspectives\, reflect on Indigenous hist
 ories and contemporary issues\, and engage in meaningful cross-cultural d
