BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Montclair State University
CATEGORIES:Arts
DESCRIPTION:\nDirected by: Katherine Wilkinson | Written by William Shakes
 peare\nTroilus and Cressida (play) is a dark\, satirical take on love and
  war during the Trojan War. Troilus and Cressida’s romance is tested when
  she is traded to the Greek camp\, while warriors and leaders on both sid
 es reveal ambition\, ego\, and moral decay. The play questions heroism\, 
 loyalty\, and what’s left of love in a world defined by conflict.\n\nMont
 clair State University Students FREE with ID at Kasser Box Office\n\n\nHo
 sted by: The College of the Arts\n\nAdditional Information can be found a
 t: https://montclair.campuslabs.com/engage/event/12607878
DTEND:20261121T020000Z
DTSTAMP:20261107T055208Z
