DESCRIPTION:KPMG is a prominent global network of independent firms delive
 ring professional audit\, tax\, and advisory services. As one of the pres
 tigious "Big Four" accounting firms\, it operates across roughly 140 coun
 tries and employs over 270\,000 professionals worldwide. The organization
  was officially formed in 1987 through the merger of Peat Marwick Interna
 tional and Klynveld Main Goerdeler\, with its name representing the initi
 als of its foundational partners. Instead of functioning as a single mult
 inational corporation\, KPMG is structured as a network of distinct\, loc
 ally managed member firms. Its primary client base includes major corpora
 tions\, government agencies\, and non-profit institutions seeking regulat
 ory compliance and strategic business consulting. Through this decentrali
 zed model\, the firm maintains a massive footprint in global financial co
 mpliance and corporate restructuring.\n\nHosted by: Accounting Society\n\
 nAdditional Information can be found at: https://montclair.campuslabs.com
 /engage/event/12807410
DTEND:20261202T200000Z
DTSTAMP:20261107T055208Z
DTSTART:20261202T190000Z
